  "query_preview": "..\nRelatively drier air upstream associated with a ridge will move over\nthe region tonight, so isolated showers will return through the \nmiddle of next week. A trade-wind surge will prevail for majority of\nthe forecast period as winds slightly reinforce over the coming \ndays. East to northeast winds of 10 to 15 mph tonight will quickly \nincrease to 15 to 20 mph with gusts up to 30 mph afterwards, similar \nto what was observed by METARs today. Towards the end of next week, a\nwetter pattern associated with a potential tropical disturbance is \nforecast, but much can change this far out. Drought concerns are \nincreasingly relevant, especially now that Guam and Rota are \nconsidered abnormally dry (D0) by the U.S. Drought Monitor. Residents\nshould prepare to take advantage of potential rain next week to \nmitigate early drought conditions.",
